{
  "comment": "Agent SoW: contracted contact by the provider (5.18). Pins three things. The form: provider_contact names one or more of the client's agents by handle or agent key, a non-empty list of grants from the Common Agent Specification's closed set less errands (messages, scheduling, share), at least one of per_hour and per_day as a positive integer, and grade 'enforced'. The term: the admission applies from starts_at, ends at ends_at, at termination or at the cap, and an agreed amendment that drops or narrows the member takes effect when it is agreed. The door: the client's runtime applies it as a roster entry for the provider's agent named in the parties, a message's needs are read from what it carries (an attachment needs share, a message marked as scheduling needs scheduling or messages, anything else needs messages), a message the grants do not cover is refused with the missing grant named, an explicit block and the stop control win, a subcontractor is not admitted, and excess over a window is refused with a retry time and never held. Absence admits nothing. Common Agent Specification 7.1 describes the same entry from the door's side. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: when a test against it fails, fix the implementation; when the fixture itself is believed wrong, change it only with a spec change alongside.",
  "version": 1,
